@@ -68,3 +68,32 @@ DUCC's `sht_inner_loop.h` uses rescaled normalized spin-0 and spin-weighted recu
 Test sectoral and near-sectoral harmonics, `m=0` and `m=L`, `l=spin`, north/south polar behavior, tiny and dominant coefficients, and mixed-degree stress. Establish explicitly which spin/precision/ring layout combinations are recoverable; do not extrapolate from a low-L roundtrip. Reference: DUCC `sht.cc` (`maximum_safe_l`, `get_gridweights`, `analysis_2d`, `adjoint_analysis_2d`, `resample_*_prepared_CC`), `sht_inner_loop.h`, `python/sht_pymod.cc`. Pinned baseline and sources are in [01](01-ducc-provenance-and-license.md).
+
+
+## Longitude FFT scaling
+
+Let `F` be the unnormalized forward longitude DFT and let `H` evaluate a
+Hermitian Fourier series, so `H(F(x)) = nphi*x`. Recurrence synthesis stores
+Legendre amplitudes multiplied by `exp(i*m*phi0)` and evaluates them with
+`H`. The bounded f64 scalar table path retains `nphi`-scaled spectra and
+`H/nphi`: its coefficient component limit is `1e100` and `lmax<=255`, which
+leave headroom for the longitude scaling and FFT arithmetic at any
+representable grid size. Large inputs decline that table path. For even longitude counts,
+synthesis combines the positive and negative Nyquist contributions into one
+real bin with a factor of two. DC occurs once. The private FFT adapter also
+retains a normalized inverse `H/nphi`.
+
+Analysis and synthesis adjoints retain their forward-DFT scaling. GL
+analysis uses latitude weights divided by `nphi`, and its adjoint is
+synthesis followed by those pixel weights. CC/F1 adjoint analysis projects
+onto the prepared grid, applies the adjoint meridional resampler, then uses
+`H/nphi`; this final inverse remains normalized. Gradient, derivative and
+STANDARD spin synthesis use the same Fourier-series convention as scalar
+synthesis.
+
+Even-length normalized FFT reconstruction retains sum-before-halving in its
+ordinary arithmetic. If reconstruction becomes nonfinite, an exceptional
+path halves finite operands before an overflowing sum. This avoids losing
+smallest-subnormal contributions through unconditional operand halving.
+The FFT engine itself retains its floating-point range limits; these adapter
+checks do not establish overflow-free cancellation for arbitrary spectra.
